WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.790
<v Instructor>So just a short lecture on Default Encryption</v>

2
00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.740
versus Bucket Policies.

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.930
So by default, now all buckets

4
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.980
are having a default encryption of SSE-S3.

5
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.810
So it's applied automatically to new objects

6
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.150
stored in your buckets, but you can change this

7
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.140
to be a different default encryption, for example, SSC KMS.

8
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.270
Nonetheless, you can also force encryption

9
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.810
by using a bucket policy to refuse any API call

10
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.710
to put an S3 object without the correct encryption headers.

11
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.430
So this is the kind of bucket policies

12
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.807
you could have in, for example, this one is saying,

13
00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:37.050
"Hey, if you do a put object

14
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.490
but you don't have the encryption header that says AWS KMS,

15
00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.960
then deny this request."

16
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.450
Or, "Hey, if you are uploading this,

17
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.740
but there is no customer side algorithm, so no SSCC,

18
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.030
then deny this object."

19
00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.380
So this is just an example,

20
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.720
but at least you see that the bucket policy

21
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.770
can also force a way to have encryption in your bucket.

22
00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.620
And by the way, bucket policies are always going to be

23
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.280
evaluated before your default encryption settings.

24
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.800
So that's it, just remember default encryption is on

25
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.740
by default with SSE S3, but you can change it

26
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.440
and you can apply a bucket policy preemptively

27
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.140
to force encryption to the one you want.

28
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.100
All right, that's it.

29
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.133
I hope you liked it and I will see you in the next lecture.

